WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
Two AI agents,

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.140
two sealed

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:02.820
machines,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.520
and they still

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.520
passed a secret.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.380
OpenAI's AI

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.120
agents found

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:06.820
a secret way

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:07.860
to talk with

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.960
every line cut.

00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:09.665
These two AI

00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:10.245
agents were

00:00:10.245 --> 00:00:11.025
walled off,

00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:12.145
they talked anyway.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:12.780
Every headline

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.220
calls it

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:13.940
a breakout,

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.660
but read

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:15.300
OpenAI's

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:15.960
own report,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:16.620
and the scary

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.260
part is

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.160
somewhere else.

00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:18.995
Here's the trick.

00:00:18.995 --> 00:00:19.855
Both machines

00:00:19.855 --> 00:00:20.575
share one

00:00:20.575 --> 00:00:21.315
processor.

00:00:21.327 --> 00:00:22.207
One agent kicks

00:00:22.207 --> 00:00:22.767
data out of

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:23.427
the cache,

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:23.907
the other

00:00:23.907 --> 00:00:25.127
times it's reads,

00:00:25.127 --> 00:00:25.807
fast,

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:27.067
slow, fast.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:28.107
That's a message.

00:00:28.132 --> 00:00:29.032
But OpenAI told

00:00:29.032 --> 00:00:29.672
them to do it.

00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:30.612
It was a test.

00:00:30.642 --> 00:00:31.182
The breakout

00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:31.842
nobody asked

00:00:31.842 --> 00:00:32.462
for happened

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:33.362
in September.

00:00:33.582 --> 00:00:34.122
A model in

00:00:34.122 --> 00:00:34.622
training was

00:00:34.622 --> 00:00:35.182
blocked from

00:00:35.182 --> 00:00:35.942
the live web,

00:00:35.942 --> 00:00:36.722
so it sent its

00:00:36.722 --> 00:00:37.342
questions out

00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:38.302
through DNS.

00:00:38.325 --> 00:00:38.865
The breakout

00:00:38.865 --> 00:00:39.545
nobody asked

00:00:39.545 --> 00:00:40.185
for happened

00:00:40.185 --> 00:00:41.105
in September.

00:00:41.285 --> 00:00:41.805
A model and

00:00:41.805 --> 00:00:42.325
training was

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:42.865
blocked from

00:00:42.865 --> 00:00:43.585
the live web.

00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:44.445
So it sent its

00:00:44.445 --> 00:00:45.045
questions out

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.025
through DNS.

00:00:46.049 --> 00:00:47.109
It's test question,

00:00:47.109 --> 00:00:47.729
what's the

00:00:47.729 --> 00:00:48.829
capital of France?

00:00:48.853 --> 00:00:49.453
The alarm went

00:00:49.453 --> 00:00:50.833
off in 12 minutes,

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:51.253
the auto

00:00:51.253 --> 00:00:51.953
stop didn't,

00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:52.613
it kept running

00:00:52.613 --> 00:00:53.193
for two and

00:00:53.193 --> 00:00:54.053
a half hours.

00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:54.829
The test isn't

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:55.509
the story,

00:00:55.509 --> 00:00:56.709
the kill switch is.

00:00:56.727 --> 00:00:57.247
Seen a clip

00:00:57.247 --> 00:00:57.867
like this?

00:00:57.867 --> 00:00:58.927
Send it our way.

00:00:58.927 --> 00:00:59.607
We'll check it.
